						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3109.msg35481#msg35481">Quote from: SKI MASK WAY on August 12, 2007, 09:39:21 pm</a></div><div class="quote"><a href="http&#58;//www.ballerstatus.com/article/editorialscolumns/2007/08/2947/" target="_blank">http://www.ballerstatus.com/article/editorialscolumns/2007/08/2947/</a><br /><br /><br />Proper<br />Education<br />Always<br />Counters<br />Exploitation<br /><br />It&#039;s NO LONGER Smart to be DUMB!<br /></div><br />I like that. <br />&nbsp;<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3109.msg35481#msg35481">Quote from: SKI MASK WAY on August 12, 2007, 09:39:21 pm</a></div><div class="quote"><a href="http&#58;//www.ballerstatus.com/article/editorialscolumns/2007/08/2947/" target="_blank">http://www.ballerstatus.com/article/editorialscolumns/2007/08/2947/</a><br /><br /><br /><br />&nbsp;EXPRESS your self, BE your self, it is your duty as an artist, but when you become an imperialist tyrant who wish to force your form of self-expression on others as the ONLY or REAL way to articulate ourselves in the world, you my friend, are no different from emperor George W. Bush and the neo-cons who wish to turn the rest of the world into the west! YOU AIN&#039;T HIP-HOP!<br /><br /><br /></div><br />Doesn&#039;t that sentence almost contradict itself. Saying to express yourself and then saying if your form of expression is a certain message to basically shut the fuck up cauz your a neo-con, Bush supporter?? Don&#039;t get me wrong, I think the argument between fake or real , not to mention the &quot; is hip hop dead or alive&quot; is moot. Hip hop is alive and well and all that it encompasses is very REAL. However, in my music, I let my opinion be known to what I believe is GOOD and BAD hip hop.  I feel morally obiged to do this because, me personally, if forced with the choice would rather have my children listen to MF DOOM then 50 cent. And really, if I have those two cd&#039;s were in front of my face and I had to choose which to throw in my cd player to show my daughter - I&#039;m gonna put on Miles Davis, Charles Mingus or Nat King Cole. Hip hop isn&#039;t dead but it is ever-evolving and the fans and the people in the game should know that although the corporation controls the channels and the funding - hip hop can be molded the way the fans and artists want it to be.<br /><br />And just so no one is thinkin I&#039;m hatin... I thought this was a great thread, a good dialogue starter with some important points.....<br />(one never can be too sure these days)</td>
